The legal texts come from InfoLEG, Ministerio de Justicia de la Nación (Argentina):

  Fuente: InfoLEG - Información Legislativa, Ministerio de Justicia de la Nación (www.infoleg.gob.ar),
  https://servicios.infoleg.gob.ar/infolegInternet/, retrieved 28 October 2026.

They are official legal texts of the Argentine Nation. InfoLEG's pages carry "Copyright 2005" and publish no licence;
the InfoLEG dataset on datos.jus.gob.ar (norm types, numbers, dates and titles used here) is published under Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), with the attribution "Fuente
https://www.infoleg.gob.ar". The copyright status of the legal texts themselves is not confirmed here; they are
reproduced with the attribution above.

Changes made by Lexifina: each text was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per line; spacing,
quotes and dashes were normalised; InfoLEG's amendment notes were removed from the text; the versions between the text
as enacted and today's consolidated text were rebuilt by applying the amending norms' own published texts; and the
versions were arranged as git commits credited to the norms that made each change. The wording of the law was not
changed. The Ministerio de Justicia does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
